<title>USA: General Host Q2 net profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>General Host Q2 net profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Host Corporation</p>
<p>		    Consolidated Summary of Sales and Earnings</p>
<p>		     (in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>						Twelve Weeks Ended</p>
<p>				    Aug 11, 1996	   Aug 13, 1995</p>
<p> Sales				 $125, 509		 $126,741</p>
<p> Income(loss) before income taxes    707		 ( 3,555)</p>
<p> Income tax (benefit) (1)		 50		    (640)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			 657		 ( 2,915)</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss) per share: (2)  </p>
<p>						0.03		  ( 0.13)</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding:	23,249		   23,254</p>
<p>						 Twenty-Eight Weeks Ended</p>
<p>				    Aug 11, 1996	   Aug 13, 1995</p>
<p> Sales				  $298,217		 $328,739</p>
<p> Income(loss) before income taxes  3,711		    8,296</p>
<p> Income tax (benefit) (1)		260			177</p>
<p> Net income (loss)		     3,451		    8,119</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss) per share: (2)</p>
<p>						0.15		     0.35</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding:	23,249		   23,252</p>
<p>(1)  The effective income tax rates used in 1996 and 1995 reflect the utilization of previously unrecognized tax benefits.  The 1995 results include the elimination of income tax reserves of $396, which were no longer required. (2) Share and per share data for 1995 have been restated to reflect a 5% stock dividend which was paid on April 5, 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
